Package: dalker
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), systemd, procps, debconf (>= 1.5), acl, dconf-cli, libglib2.0-bin, gstreamer1.0-tools, gstreamer1.0-pipewire, pkexec | policykit-1, libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libgtk-3-0
Recommends: xserver-xorg-core
Maintainer: Dalker <dalker@localhost>
Description: Remote desktop agent (WebRTC) with browser client
 Dalker streams the desktop to a web browser over WebRTC and accepts remote
 mouse and keyboard input. It runs as a background service, follows the login
 screen and the user session (Xorg, or GNOME on Wayland through its screen-cast
 service), and draws a red border around the screen whenever someone is connected
 (a GNOME Shell extension on Wayland). Web access, the web client password and
 the MCP server for AI agents (with its access tokens) are set on the host only,
 with the "Dalker Settings" app.
